      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Leucine acts as a potent signaling molecule that directly stimulates the mTOR pathway, a key regulator of muscle protein synthesis. It functions as an amino acid sensor, binding to and activating upstream elements necessary to switch on the mTOR cascade. Consuming a caloric surplus provides the necessary energy substrate to support the anabolic processes activated by sufficient amino acids like leucine. This positive energy balance helps drive a positive nitrogen balance, which is crucial for the net accumulation of lean muscle mass.",
